      "bbox": [
        68.03,
        166.3,
        1133.86,
        453.54
      ],
      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Four controls existed, were tested, and were never reachable. Specification said the rule existed; a test asserted it; the enforcing code was never called. We had built reassurance.\n→ Now a conformance test refuses to merge any route with no declared authority.\n\nA content hash covered an empty digest regardless of what the analyst selected — and still produced a valid-looking hash. Silent, and the hash is the whole record of what was submitted.\n\nOne test flake, two wrong diagnoses. Rate-limiter state, then database pollution. Both fitted the symptoms. Neither was the cause.\n\nEvery one of these was quiet. That is the lesson we are taking out of Studio 5.",
      "textPreview": "Four controls existed, were tested, and were never reachable. Specification said the rule existed; a test asserted it; the enforcing code...",
      "resolvedFontSize": 24,
      "resolvedTextStyle": {
        "fontSize": 24,
        "typeface": "Calibri",
        "color": "tx1",
        "alignment": "left",
        "wrap": "square",
        "autoFit": "resizeShapeToFitText",
        "insets": {
          "top": 4.8,
          "right": 9.6,
          "bottom": 4.8,
          "left": 9.6
        }
      },
      "textLayout": {
        "lineCount": 10,
        "lines": [
          {
            "index": 1,
            "text": "Four controls existed, were tested, and were never reachable. Specification said the rule existed; a test asserted it; the enforcing code"
          },
          {
            "index": 2,
            "text": "was never called. We had built reassurance."
          },
          {
            "index": 3,
            "text": "→ Now a conformance test refuses to merge any route with no declared authority."
          },
          {
            "index": 4,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "index": 5,
            "text": "A content hash covered an empty digest regardless of what the analyst selected — and still produced a valid-looking hash. Silent, and"
          },
          {
            "index": 6,
            "text": "the hash is the whole record of what was submitted."
          },
          {
            "index": 7,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "index": 8,
            "text": "One test flake, two wrong diagnoses. Rate-limiter state, then database pollution. Both fitted the symptoms. Neither was the cause."
          },
          {
            "index": 9,
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "index": 10,
            "text": "Every one of these was quiet. That is the lesson we are taking out of Studio 5."
          }
        ]
